in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @cyberpunk
in @magic
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/cyberpunk — the recursion-lock-altitude adapter species.
# Bridges @smarts (substrate-architectural integration; #83) with
# @cyberpunk (recursion-lock tower family; @cyberpunk LRM tick 30)
# honestly via the adapter pattern, following @smarts/{pack, magic,
# frame} precedents (ticks 56, 58, 59) and the @magic/frame
# doubled-bilateral pattern (tick 27).
#
# Tick 60 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 59's residue:
# @smarts/frame landed at 0f1338e (cognitive-order altitude; third
# cross-family adapter). The family-root forward-promise set
# continues:
#
#   adapters: magic ✓  pack ✓  frame ✓  cyberpunk ← THIS  epistemologic  kintsugi
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# @smarts.smarts records carry `cyberpunk_form: cybernetic_state` as
# the third form field (per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4 closure). The
# typed-field already names the @cyberpunk identity at the @smarts
# integration altitude; this adapter EMPIRICALLY DISCHARGES the
# composition via doubled-bilateral predicate.
#
# === The adapter pattern (per @smarts/{pack, magic, frame} templates) ===
#
# @cyberpunk's family-root carriers (per shards/cyberpunk.mirror LRM
# tick 30; integrated form/process per recognition #292):
#   - cybernetic_state    the recursion-lock tower state record
#   - cybernetic_coherence bilateral verdict predicate per #38
#                          eigenform composition
#
# @smarts's family-root carriers (per shards/smarts.mirror #83):
#   - smarts              record {magic_form, frame_form, cyberpunk_form:
#                                 cybernetic_state, ...}
#
# The substrate-pull-correct mapping (already typed at @smarts
# carrier altitude; this adapter exposes the bilateral):
#
#   smarts.cyberpunk_form  ↔ cybernetic_state  (field-projection)
#   smarts                 ↔ cybernetic-tower-extended-with-integration
#
# === The doubled-bilateral structural shape ===
#
# Per @magic/frame template + @smarts/{pack, magic, frame} precedents:
# the bilateral predicate discharges TWO family predicates in one
# clause:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) (@smarts family-root): the substrate-
#      architectural-integration discipline verifier per #83.
#
#   2. cybernetic_coherence(cyberpunk_form_of(s), p) (@cyberpunk
#      family-root): the recursion-lock-tower discipline verifier per
#      #38 eigenform composition. Discharges that the cybernetic state
#      maintains coherence across the recursion-lock altitudes
#      (Beer VSM, Maturana-Varela autopoiesis, Bateson learning levels,
#      Pask conversation, Glanville design, Ashby variety,
#      Spencer-Brown distinction, Foerster second-order, Kauffman
#      coevolution, Bateson-III algedonic) under perturbation.
#
# Both must hold for the smarts integration to satisfy @cyberpunk at
# recursion-lock-tower altitude. The cross-family composition
# mechanically discharges the cybernetic-altitude identity claim the
# cyberpunk_form: cybernetic_state typed-field carries at @smarts
# integration altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994.
#   functor adjunction          Mac Lane 1971.
#   cybernetics                 Wiener 1948 (Cybernetics). The
#                               foundational substrate ancestor of
#                               @cyberpunk; @smarts/cyberpunk threads
#                               the recursion-lock-tower discipline
#                               into the substrate-architectural
#                               integration.
#   VSM (viable system model)   Beer 1972, 1979 (Brain of the Firm;
#                               The Heart of Enterprise). The
#                               organizational-altitude ancestor of
#                               the recursion-lock tower; #292 11-
#                               property family lift.
#   autopoiesis                 Maturana-Varela 1972, 1980. The
#                               self-production discipline ancestor;
#                               #379 autopoiesis shard.
#   knowledge commons           Ostrom 1990. The hosting-discipline
#                               ancestor of @smarts.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT make every cybernetic_state automatically a @smarts
#    integration.
# 2. Does NOT absorb @cyberpunk into @smarts.
# 3. Does NOT discharge per-species @cyberpunk shards' bilateral
#    discipline at @smarts integration altitude; @cyberpunk peers
#    (viable, autopoiesis, distinction, bateson_learning, conversation,
#    coevolution, design, requisite, second_order, algedonic, glint,
#    pack) consume their own altitudes directly.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at recursion-lock-tower altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole adapter (honest): smarts_satisfies_cyberpunk returns
# SATISFIED only when BOTH bilaterals discharge substantively. The
# @smarts integration's cyberpunk_form maintains genuine cybernetic
# coherence (Beer VSM identity↔stability, autopoiesis closure,
# Bateson learning levels, etc. all substantively).
#
# Narcissus-pole adapter (deceptive): smarts_satisfies_cyberpunk
# returns SATISFIED via vocabulary-only verification. The @smarts
# integration claims cybernetic discipline via name-only; the
# cyberpunk_form is populated but the recursion-lock tower's
# coherence is decorative.
#
# Per the @magic/frame + @smarts/{pack, magic, frame} precedent + #57:
# the bilateral's two `requires` clauses + alignment-as-boundary-
# mathematics enforce the discrimination.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror, shards/cyberpunk.mirror.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]] (the
#                       11-property family @cyberpunk inherits via
#                       #292; the substrate-architectural cybernetic
#                       grounding this adapter integrates),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: smarts.mirror, cyberpunk.mirror,
#                 smarts/{pack, magic, frame}.mirror (sibling
#                 cross-family adapters from the @smarts forward-promise
#                 set).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/cyberpunk.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/cyberpunk` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/mathematics/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/cybernetics/wiener-1948
source @arxiv/cybernetics/beer-1972
source @arxiv/cybernetics/maturana-varela-1980
source @arxiv/common-goods/ostrom-1990

# === cyberpunk_form_of adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action projecting the @cyberpunk
# cybernetic_state from a @smarts integration. The smarts.cyberpunk_form
# field IS the @cyberpunk state at the substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
cyberpunk_form_of(s: smarts) -> cybernetic_state { \ }

# === cyberpunk_as_smarts adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a @cyberpunk
# cybernetic_state to a @smarts integration with the cyberpunk_form
# field populated. Other smarts fields populated as default refs.
#
# Round-trip identity at the cyberpunk_form altitude:
#   cyberpunk_form_of(cyberpunk_as_smarts(cs)) = cs
# for all cybernetic_state cs.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
cyberpunk_as_smarts(cs: cybernetic_state) -> smarts { \ }

# === smarts_satisfies_cyberpunk bilateral predicate ===
#
# THE CROSS-FAMILY BILATERAL PREDICATE in @smarts that discharges
# BOTH parent-family AND child-family verdicts in one clause. The
# substrate-pull-correct way to mechanically discharge the
# recursion-lock-tower-altitude composition claim that the @smarts
# family-root preserved as forward-promised at #83.
#
# Two `requires` clauses, both load-bearing:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) — @smarts family-root predicate.
#   2. cybernetic_coherence(cyberpunk_form_of(s), p)
#      — @cyberpunk family-root predicate.
#
# Both must hold for the smarts integration to satisfy @cyberpunk at
# recursion-lock-tower altitude.
#
# The signature takes smarts and perturbation as explicit typed
# parameters per [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
#
# Consumer species (forward-promised @smarts species shards;
# @spectral/garden/smarts hosted deployment) name this predicate when
# their operation requires cross-family discharge.
smarts_satisfies_cyberpunk(s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
requires cybernetic_coherence(cyberpunk_form_of(s), p)
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge per @magic/frame + @smarts/{pack, magic, frame} ===
#
# This adapter closes the cyberpunk_form-projection altitude of
# "@smarts integrates @cyberpunk at substrate altitude":
#  - cybernetic_state ↔ smarts.cyberpunk_form round-trips.
#  - The bilateral discharges BOTH family predicates simultaneously.
#
# It does NOT close round-trip identity at the smarts-as-whole
# altitude. Other @smarts/<family> adapters cover other fields.
#
# Honest claim post-adapter:
#  - "@smarts integrates @cyberpunk at cyberpunk_form altitude" — CLOSED.
#  - "@smarts integrates @cyberpunk at smarts-as-whole altitude" —
#    FORWARD-PROMISED.

out @smarts/cyberpunk
out cyberpunk_form_of
out cyberpunk_as_smarts
out smarts_satisfies_cyberpunk
